Z||000000||Motorhead||05-06-2000||05:43 AM||||I just picked up an '84 coupe to drive while I finish my '86, so I'm going through the car to get everything working.<BR>My problem is no power to the headlight switch.  The wiring diagram shows two sources, an orange wire from the fuse box for the running lights, and a red from a fusable link.  I went to check the links behind the battery like in the '86, and they're not there.  Am I out of it here or are they in a different place on '84s?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||05-06-2000||09:42 AM||||They are in a different place, they are coming out of the starter. It is a pain in the --- but we just fixed one with the same thing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Motorhead||05-06-2000||10:03 AM||||Thanks alot, I scoured that car yesterday looking for them.  Never thought to get UNDER the car to look for them.  <BR>With the number of splices, reroutes and miles of electrical tape used on this car by a previous owner I seem to be spending most of my time looking for shorts.  Heat/ac fan was powered be the headlight circuit for instance. Go figure!<BR>Thanks again for the info.  Great help!<P>Mike||||reg||1
